<h1>cbodotnet</h1>
<p>Community .NET SDK builds for glibc Linux x64 and aarch64, independently of the upstream support lifecycle.</p>
<p class="status" aria-label="CI/CD workflow status">
<a href="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/checks.yml"><img src="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/checks.yml/badge.svg?branch=main" alt="Repository checks status"></a>
<a href="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/sdk-matrix.yml"><img src="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/sdk-matrix.yml/badge.svg?branch=main" alt="Linux AArch64 SDK build status"></a>
<a href="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/sdk-x64.yml"><img src="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/sdk-x64.yml/badge.svg?branch=main" alt="Linux x64 SDK build status"></a>
<a href="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/upstream-sdk.yml"><img src="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/upstream-sdk.yml/badge.svg?branch=main" alt="Upstream SDK tracking and publication status"></a>
<a href="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/publish-releases.yml"><img src="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/publish-releases.yml/badge.svg?branch=main" alt="Release publication status"></a>
<a href="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/pages.yml"><img src="{{REPOSITORY_URL}}/actions/workflows/pages.yml/badge.svg?branch=main" alt="Download pages deployment status"></a>
</p>
<h2>Downloads</h2>
<p>Each build provides the SDK, the sources actually used, and verification evidence. Select <strong>tar.gz</strong> to download an SDK.</p>
<div class="downloads">
<table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">SDK version</th><th scope="col">Linux x64</th><th scope="col">Linux aarch64</th><th scope="col">Verification</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{DOWNLOAD_ROWS}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h2>Using a build</h2>
<p>Verify the SHA-256 checksum, extract the SDK archive, and run <code>./dotnet --info</code>. These are glibc builds; distribution libraries are still required. Native checks cover Ubuntu 22.04, Ubuntu 24.04 and Debian 13. .NET 5 and Core 3.x require the recorded OpenSSL 1.1 dependencies; Core 3.x on Debian 13 also uses ICU 66.</p>
<p>These are community builds, without Microsoft support. Construction details and any reused upstream binary inputs are recorded in the release evidence.</p>
